          ( 1 - ( E / N ) ) < ( ( X ` j ) ` t ) ) $.
    $( This lemma proves that for all ` t ` in ` T ` there is a ` j ` as in the
       proof of [BrosowskiDeutsh] p. 91 (at the bottom of page 91 and at the
       top of page 92):  (j-4/3) * &epsilon; < f(t) <= (j-1/3) * &epsilon; ,
       g(t) < (j+1/3) * &epsilon;, and g(t) > (j-4/3) * &epsilon;.  Here ` E `
       is used to represent &epsilon; in the paper.  (Contributed by Glauco
       Siliprandi, 20-Apr-2017.) $)
