    fourier.dmdv $e |- ( ( -u _pi (,) _pi ) \ dom G ) e. Fin $.
    fourier.dvcn $e |- G e. ( dom G -cn-> CC ) $.
    fourier.rlim $e |- ( x e. ( ( -u _pi [,) _pi ) \ dom G ) -> ( ( G |` ( x
       (,) +oo ) ) limCC x ) =/= (/) ) $.
    fourier.llim $e |- ( x e. ( ( -u _pi (,] _pi ) \ dom G ) -> ( ( G |` ( -oo
       (,) x ) ) limCC x ) =/= (/) ) $.
    fourier.x $e |- X e. RR $.
    fourier.l $e |- L e. ( ( F |` ( -oo (,) X ) ) limCC X ) $.
    fourier.r $e |- R e. ( ( F |` ( X (,) +oo ) ) limCC X ) $.
    fourier.a $e |- A = ( n e. NN0 |-> ( S. ( -u _pi (,) _pi ) ( ( F ` x ) x. (
       cos ` ( n x. x ) ) ) _d x / _pi ) ) $.
    fourier.b $e |- B = ( n e. NN |-> ( S. ( -u _pi (,) _pi ) ( ( F ` x ) x. (
       sin ` ( n x. x ) ) ) _d x / _pi ) ) $.
    $( Fourier series convergence for periodic, piecewise smooth functions.
       The series converges to the average value of the left and the right
       limit of the function.  Thus, if the function is continuous at a given
